bin "tv"
about "Synced 24/7 TV channel: an LLM picks Jellyfin items and new YouTube videos, every browser on /<secret>/ plays the same frame at the same moment; /<secret>/schedule shows the plan and lets editors put items at fixed times"

flag "-config" help="JSON config: listen, state_dir, cache_dir, cache_max_bytes, secret_file, jellyfin_url, jellyfin_key_file, youtube_videos_per_channel (newest videos per channel the picker may choose, default 15), youtube_share (fraction 0..1 of the picked airtime that is YouTube, topped up past the LLM's answer; default 0 = up to the LLM), channel_suggestions_per_week (YouTube channels similar to the current ones the LLM adds to the suggestions once a week, checked like api/channels/suggest and marked \"by\": \"llm\"; default 0 = off), yt_dlp, yt_dlp_args, ffmpeg, llm_url (OpenAI-compatible), llm_model, llm_key_file, look_ahead (how far ahead the schedule is planned and prepared, default 3h), admin_key_file (bearer key for the editor endpoints: POST api/skip, api/schedule/*, api/channels/{add,remove,approve,reject}, api/slots/{add,remove} and GET api/search), oidc_issuer, oidc_client_id_file, oidc_redirect_url (optional login for editors besides the admin key: a public PKCE client; the redirect URL's path, outside the secret prefix, finishes the login; cookies are signed with state_dir/cookie.key), jellyseerr_url, jellyseerr_key_file, requests_per_day (new movies the LLM requests through Jellyseerr once a day, default 0 = off), audio_languages (preferred audio track languages like [\"en\", \"de\"], first match wins, else the first audio track), subtitle_languages (YouTube subtitle languages like [\"en\", \"de\"], auto-generated where there is no manual track; Jellyfin items get all their text subtitles), sponsorblock_categories (SponsorBlock categories like [\"sponsor\"] cut out of YouTube videos and their subtitles, default none; uncut if SponsorBlock is unreachable). The YouTube channels and the slots (items at a fixed time, api/slots) live in state_dir/state.json, the channels managed over api/channels (suggest is public, the rest admin); rejected suggestions and removed channels cannot be suggested again" required=#true {
  arg "<file>"
}
